Description: Linux and Windows virtual machines on Qualcomm Gunyah
 GunyahVM combines its pinned crosvm build, GTK and CLI frontends, ordinary-user supervision,
 Windows media preparation, guest drivers, UEFI firmware and host integration.
 Windows requires an owner-provided ARM64 ISO and licence.
